# Typing on the PC (xnuhost --input-script FILE; format: src/input_script.c): after the boot, go Home, open Search (a
# swipe down in the middle of the Home Screen, which brings up the keyboard), then tap keys of the keyboard's top two
# rows and the space bar: 100 keys, 1.4 a second (70 s); then the same again from Home. For a before and an after
# run of a fix that is about typing (kbd's and the search's process in the oneios-cpu, oneios-perf and oneios-top
# lines). The axes are input-demo.script's (a 1440 x 3120 panel). The key places are a 6.9-inch iPhone's keyboard at
# its proportions (rows at about 75 % and 80 % of the height, the space bar at 91 %), not measured on a screenshot: a tap
# that misses a key types nothing or another key, which does not matter for a load.
abs 0x2f 0 9             # ABS_MT_SLOT
abs 0x39 0 65535         # ABS_MT_TRACKING_ID
abs 0x35 0 1439 10       # ABS_MT_POSITION_X
abs 0x36 0 3119 10       # ABS_MT_POSITION_Y
wait 1080000             # 18 min: SpringBoard and the Home Screen under qemu (before `ready`: `repeat` does not wait again)
ready
swipe 720 3100 720 1500 300   # up from the bottom edge: Home (from the Lock Screen too)
wait 5000
swipe 720 1100 720 1900 300   # down in the middle of the Home Screen: Search and its keyboard
wait 20000
tap 72 2340
wait 700
tap 216 2340
wait 700
tap 360 2340
wait 700
tap 504 2340
wait 700
tap 648 2340
wait 700
tap 792 2340
wait 700
tap 936 2340
wait 700
tap 1080 2340
wait 700
tap 1224 2340
wait 700
tap 1368 2340
wait 700
tap 144 2500
wait 700
tap 288 2500
wait 700
tap 432 2500
wait 700
tap 576 2500
wait 700
tap 720 2840             # space
wait 700
tap 864 2500
wait 700
tap 1008 2500
wait 700
tap 1152 2500
wait 700
tap 1296 2500
wait 700
tap 720 2840
wait 700
